Lock screen fingerprint: no 30-second scan limit. pam_fprintd's default timeout ended the scan
every 30s while the lock sat idle, which reset the reader (a touch during the ~1s restart was
missed) and counted as an error, so after three timeouts (~90s) the lock flashed "Fingerprint
reader isn't responding" although it was fine. timeout=-1 keeps one scan running until a
finger, unlocking or sleep ends it.
--- a/assets/pam.d/fprint
+++ b/assets/pam.d/fprint
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 #%PAM-1.0
 
-auth    required    pam_fprintd.so  max-tries=1
+auth    required    pam_fprintd.so  max-tries=1 timeout=-1
